ystems and Smart Manufacturing","degree":"M.E","fam":"mech","at":["Y","",""],"note":"Sponsored program: admission also needs an industry-panel interview"},{"prog":"Quantum Information Processing","degree":"M.E","fam":"other","at":["","Y",""],"note":""},{"prog":"Quantum Science and Technology","degree":"M.E","fam":"other","at":["","Y",""],"note":""},{"prog":"M.Pharm with specialization in Pharmaceutics","degree":"M.Pharm","fam":"bio","at":["Y","","HD"],"note":""},{"prog":"M.Pharm with specialization in Pharmacology","degree":"M.Pharm","fam":"bio","at":["Y","","HD"],"note":""}]},"official":[{"k":"Two routes","text":"Admission is on a GATE score (GATE 2024, 2025 or 2026; GPAT for M.Pharm) or on marks in the BITS HD test, and a candidate can ask to be considered on either or both. Each program keeps two merit lists, one per route, and fills at most half its seats from each; seats one list leaves empty go to the other. Admission is on merit alone.","src":{"k":"official","l":"BITS Pilani Higher Degree (M.E./M.Pharm.) admissions brochure 2026-27","u":"https://admissions.bits-pilani.ac.in/HD/downloads/HD_Brochure_2026_27.pdf","f":"reports/BITS/BITS_Pilani/admissions/2026/HD_Brochure_2026-27.pdf","p":6}},{"k":"The HD test","text":"Test I (45 minutes, 30 questions: 15 core mathematics, 15 English and logical reasoning) is for everyone. Test II (105 minutes, 70 questions) is in the candidate's discipline. Software Systems and Environmental Engineering set a Special Test (60 minutes, 50 questions) in its place. Each question is worth 3 marks and a wrong answer costs 1, so the most anyone can score is 300 (Test I + Test II) or 240 (Test I + a Special Test).","src":{"k":"official","l":"BITS Pilani Higher Degree (M.E./M.Pharm.) admissions brochure 2026-27","u":"https://admissions.bits-pilani.ac.in/HD/downloads/HD_Brochure_2026_27.pdf","f":"reports/BITS/BITS_Pilani/admissions/2026/HD_Brochure_2026-27.pdf","p":15}},{"k":"Money","text":"Through GATE: the AICTE GATE scholarship plus a tuition fee waiver of Rs 13,400 a month during the semester. Through the HD test: a stipend of Rs 13,400 a month during the semester. Either way, 8 to 10 hours a week as a teaching assistant.","src":{"k":"official","l":"BITS Pilani Higher Degree (M.E./M.Pharm.) admissions brochure 2026-27","u":"https://admissions.bits-pilani.ac.in/HD/downloads/HD_Brochure_2026_27.pdf","f":"reports/BITS/BITS_Pilani/admissions/2026/HD_Brochure_2026-27.pdf","p":7}},{"k":"Fees","text":"Tuition Rs 2,91,500 a semester in 2026-27, rising 5% a year for the batch, and Rs 1,02,000 for a summer term. Admission fee Rs 64,100; hostel Rs 36,000 a semester. The same at all three campuses.","src":{"k":"official","l":"BITS Pilani Higher Degree schedule of fees 2026-27","u":"https://admissions.bits-pilani.ac.in/HD/downloads/Fee_Structure_AY_2026-27.pdf","f":"reports/BITS/BITS_Pilani/admissions/2026/Fee_Structure_AY_2026-27.pdf","p":1}},{"k":"Eligibility","text":"At least 60% in the qualifying degree.","src":{"k":"official","l":"BITS Pilani Higher Degree (M.E./M.Pharm.) admissions brochure 2026-27","u":"https://admissions.bits-pilani.ac.in/HD/downloads/HD_Brochure_2026_27.pdf","f":"reports/BITS/BITS_Pilani/admissions/2026/HD_Brochure_2026-27.pdf","p":5}}],"campuses":["Pilani","Goa","Hyderabad"],"progs":["Communication Engineering","Computer Science","Design Engineering","Embedded Systems","Microelectronics","Civil: Structural Engineering","Biotechnology","Civil: Infrastructure Engineering and Management","Civil: Transportation Engineering","M.Pharm Pharmaceutical Chemistry","M.Pharm Pharmacology","Manufacturing Systems Engineering","Mechanical","Software Systems","Chemical"],"progFam":["ece","cse","mech","vlsi","vlsi","civil","bio","civil","civil","bio","bio","mech","mech","cse","chem"],"measures":{"gate":["GATE score",1000],"gpat":["GPAT score",1000],"hd":["HD marks",300],"hd_ss":["HD marks, Test 1 + Special Test",240]},"offers":[[2023,1,0,"GATE","gate",1,2,501,504.5,508],[2023,1,0,"GATE","gate",0,2